{"results":[{"rowIndex":309,"group":"4","grade":8,"candidate":"C4","reason":"Two women in green are cut out; then the remaining pair is held two spots apart on the line.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":309,"group":"5","grade":8,"candidate":"C5","reason":"The two women in green are cut out before the remaining pair is held two spots apart on the line.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":309,"group":"6","grade":1,"candidate":"C6","reason":"It makes “hold” a nonfinite complement of “cut” instead of a second imperative introduced by “then.”","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":310,"group":"2","grade":3,"candidate":"C2","reason":"It attaches “from Refund” to the pull clause but treats “long enough” as an entity and loses the arrow’s purpose of being readable.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":310,"group":"4","grade":7,"candidate":"C4","reason":"It captures the two requests and their purposes, but the separate “read” clause is not linked to the arrow being long enough.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":310,"group":"5","grade":7,"candidate":"C5","reason":"It captures pulling Confirm away from Refund and leaving a small even gap, but leaves “to read” unattached to “long enough.”","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":310,"group":"6","grade":1,"candidate":"C6","reason":"It misreads the name Refund as a predicate, and the readability clause is unattached.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":310,"group":"7","grade":3,"candidate":"C7","reason":"It groups the arrow’s becoming long enough with the separate instruction to leave a gap under the first “so.”","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":311,"group":"0","grade":8,"candidate":"C0","reason":"Draw a small dog in a red scarf on the left.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":311,"group":"1","grade":8,"candidate":"C1","reason":"The dog is small, wears a red scarf, and is to be drawn on the left.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":311,"group":"2","grade":3,"candidate":"C2","reason":"It puts the drawing in the scarf and the scarf o