,"candidate":"C7","reason":"It represents the missing piece with solid green surface colour on the surface chart, followed by a separate legend on the right.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":312,"group":"8","grade":1,"candidate":"C8","reason":"It turns the fragment into a declarative clause with “colour” as predicate and misplaces the chart and surface roles.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":313,"group":"4","grade":8,"candidate":"C4","reason":"The speaker wants a canyon camp in the sun at noon, elaborated by four cactuses, a lizard, and a guide.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":313,"group":"5","grade":3,"candidate":"C5","reason":"It includes the camp itself as a fourth member of the list that elaborates the camp.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":313,"group":"6","grade":1,"candidate":"C6","reason":"It reads “camp” as a verb and “canyon” as the wanted object rather than “a canyon camp.”","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":314,"group":"0","grade":3,"candidate":"C0","reason":"It attaches “centred” to level 1 rather than to the Chapter heading being updated.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":314,"group":"1","grade":3,"candidate":"C1","reason":"It treats “centred” as a modifier of level 1 rather than a property of the heading.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":314,"group":"5","grade":3,"candidate":"C5","reason":"It assigns the object name Outline and level 1, but attaches “centred” to the level rather than the heading.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":314,"group":"6","grade":3,"candidate":"C6","reason":"It links level 1 to the heading but makes “centred” a modifier of the level.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":314,"group":"7","grade":1,"candidate":"C7","reason":"It misreads “heading” and “name” as predicates instead of the Chapter heading and its object name.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":315,"group":"1","grade":3,"candidate":"C1","reason":"It misreads “tent facing” as an entity and makes “left” a result of wanting.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":315,"group":"2","grade":3,"candidate":"C2","reason":"It links the pond behind “tent facing” but loses the duck’s leftward facing direction.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":315,"group":"4","grade":8,"candidate":"C4","reason":"The speaker wants the duck on the pond behind the tent, facing left, as drawn so far.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":315,"group":"5","grade":8,"candidate":"C5","reason":"The speaker wants the duck on the pond behind the tent facing left; “as drawn so far” modifies that depiction.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":315,"group":"8","grade":3,"candidate":"C8","reason":"It attaches “facing left” to the tent rather than the duck.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":316,"group":"0","grade":8,"candidate":"C0","reason":"It asks to make Biscuit red and ends with thanks.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":316,"group":"1","grade":8,"candidate":"C1","reason":"The polite imperative makes Biscuit red, followed by thanks.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":316,"group":"2","grade":8,"candidate":"C2","reason":"It asks to make Biscuit red and includes the closing thanks.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":316,"group":"3","grade":8,"candidate":"C3","reason":"Biscuit is the object of “make,” red is the result, and “Thanks” is a gratitude fragment.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":316,"group":"4","grade":1,"candidate":"C4","reason":"It incorrectly treats “Please” as a separate imperative predicate.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":316,"group":"5","grade":8,"candidate":"C5","reason":"The request is to make Biscuit red, followed by thanks.","referenceIssue":null},{"rowIndex":316,"group":"6","grade":8,"candidate":"C6","reason":"It correctly represents the polite request to make Biscuit red and the closing thanks.","referenceIssue":null}]}
